\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on May 25  \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2005\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, May 25 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE ON EURO ADOPTION PLAN  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry will hold a news conference on Slovakia's euro adoption plan.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK C.BANK HOLDS RATES, MORE WARNINGS ON WAGES  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left all key interest rates on hold for the third consecutive month on Tuesday, but reiterated warnings about fast wage growth and possible risks to medium-term inflation goals.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK C.BANK SAYS SOLD 315 MLN EUROS IN APRIL  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) sold 315 million euros ($398 million) on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at halting a weakening of the crown.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SLOVAK\b0 \highlight\uc2  JAN-MARCH C/A SWINGS TO SKK 5.3 BLN GAP  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's current account showed a deficit of 5.3 billion crowns ($170.3 million) in January-March, compared with a 5.3 billion surplus in the same period last year.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK C.BANK REPO DRAINS SKK 158.3 BLN FROM MKT  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accepted all bids in a regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday, draining 158.267 billion crowns ($5.1 billion) of surplus liquidity from the market.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK END-FEB FOREIGN DEBT JUMPS  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's gross foreign debt jumped to $26.583 billion at the end of February, from $23.973 billion at the end of January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                         [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                        [TOP/EAST]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on May 25|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050525e15p000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
