\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown steady, seen testing stronger levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2005\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, May 3 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par held steady against the euro on Tuesday, with dealers saying\par they saw a gradual shift to stronger levels if neighbouring\par markets remained stabilised.\par  \par     The crown closed at 39.270/290 to the euro, its main\par reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , slightly stronger from Monday's 39.280/310.\par     The crown fell sharply from all-time highs of 37.510 per\par euro seen early in March as short-term capital fled central\par European markets.\par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stopped the crown's decline\par with direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when it approached the psychological\par level of 40.000 per euro on Friday.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stopped the weakening trend, and it\par renewed demand for crowns," said VUB Bank trader Laco Benedek.\par     Benedek said he saw 39.200 per euro as the near-term target\par level unless the neighbouring markets started falling again.\par     But dealers saw good support for the crown near\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 39.700-39.900 to the euro even in case of turbulence in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 region, focusing mainly on the Polish market, as they expected  \par \par \uc2 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act again to prevent sharp crown fall.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers said the crown could get an impulse to firm  \par \par \uc2 if South Korean tyre maker Hankook Tire decides to  \par \par \uc2 build a planned 500-million-euro factory in Slovakia.  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Pavol Rusko said on Monday the government  \par \par \uc2 had met Hankook conditions for investing in Slovakia and that he  \par \par \uc2 was expecting a positive answer from the company in the near  \par \par \uc2 future.  \par \par \uc2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1415 GMT -  \par \par \uc2 Crown/euro at 39.270/290 vs 39.280/310 on Monday  \par \par \uc2 Crown/dollar at 30.480/500 vs 30.610/650  \par \par \uc2 5-yr yield at 3.401/102 pct vs 3.203/069 pct  \par \par \uc2 9-yr yield at 3.691/491 pct vs 3.729/601 pct  \par \par \uc2 -.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050503e15300422\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
