\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown weakens as region continues to fall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, March 15 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par extended its fall and touched a three-week low to the euro on\par Tuesday, driven by continued outflow of foreign capital from\par European emerging markets, dealers said.\par     The crown has lost 0.9 percent versus the euro this week,\par closing the Tuesday's session at 37.920/930 to the euro, its\par main reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The regional influence continues to drive the crown. Once\par this factor disappears, the crown will return to stronger\par levels," said a Tatra Banka trader Jozef Bozek.\par  Dealers said Slovakia was viewed by investors as\par economically sound, which supported the crown and prevented a\par sharper decline.\par  The neighbouring Polish zloty has lost 2 percent to the euro\par since Friday's close as investors shifted their focus from\par emerging markets to rebounding dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The current outflow of funds from the region and crown\par easing have given breathing room for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par which had repeatedly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks to halt the\par crown firming.\par     Traders have estimated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have bought\par hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worth around 2 billion euros in direct\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year aimed at slowing crown advance.\par  \par     The bank last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the market early last week, when\par the crown hit an all-time high of 37.510 to the euro.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1545 GMT--------------------\par Crown/euro  at 37.920/930 vs 37.800/810 on Monday\par Crown/dollar  at 28.430/490 vs 28.250/280\par ----------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050315e13f00aue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
