\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown in tight range, region slows firming.  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 16:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, March 11 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par closed slightly stronger versus the euro on Friday, but dealers\par said investors' uncertainty about the trend on bigger markets in\par the region would slow the unit's advance in the near term.\par     The crown was at all-time highs of 37.510 to the euro, its\par main reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , early in the week, but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and investors' retreat from central European\par markets pulled the unit to weaker levels.\par  The crown found good support at 37.700 where some foreign\par players and corporate clients opened new positions.\par     But the unit was unlikely to move to its record highs\par quickly again until Polish and Hungarian markets rebound from\par this week's fall, after the crown ignored even\par faster-than-expected GDP growth published on Thursday.\par     "The long-term trend has not changed, more crown\par strengthening is still expected," said Tatra Banka trader Jozef\par Bozek.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "But from the medium term perspective, the trend can be\par slowed down by the regional mood, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has repeatedly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly\par on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market this year to slow crown firming,\par saying the unit's fast advance is harmful to the economy.\par     Traders said the crown should not show any significant\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reaction to the release of January foreign trade data on Monday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 as flows of funds in and out of the region prevailed over local  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic fundamentals at present.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1503 GMT-  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/euro at 37.580/600 vs 37.650/570 on Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/dollar at 27.950/980 vs 28.045/095  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050311e13b00bwd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
