\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on March 9.  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, March 9 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE JAN RETAIL SALES DATA  \par \par \uc2 The statistics office will release January retail sales data.  \par \par \uc2 GOVT TO HOLD REGULAR WEEKLY MEETING  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak government will hold its regular weekly meeting.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK CBANK ACCEPTS SKK 109.99 BLN IN 2-WK REPO  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) accepted bids worth 109.99 billion crowns ($3.86 billion) in the regular two-week repo out of total demand of 181.80 billion, the bank's data showed.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK SAYS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  AGAINST STRONG CROWN  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time this week to slow crown firming.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK JAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT +5.5 PCT Y/Y  \par \par \uc2 Slovak industrial output rose by real 5.5 percent on the year in January, after a revised 0.3 percent increase in the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK JAN CONSTRUCTION OUTPUT +23.7 PCT Y/Y  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's construction output rose by 23.7 percent on the year in January, accelerating from 19.4 percent growth in December.  \par \par \uc2 VOLKSWAGEN'S SLOVAK UNIT SALES DOWN ON LOWER OUTPUT  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit of German car producer Volkswagen (VOWG.DE) said its 2004 sales dropped to 173 billion crowns ( $6.1 billion), from 183 billion in the previous year amid lower output.  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countri