\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on March 8.  \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, March 8 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK TO HOLD ITS REGULAR WEEKLY MEETING   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making Bank Board will hold its weekly meeting to decide on the result of the regular two-week repo tender.   \par \par \uc2  STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE JAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT   \par \par \uc2  The statistics office will release January industrial production and construction output data. The market expects 2.4 percent annual growth in industrial output.   \par \par \uc2  FINMIN SAYS PENSION REFORM WON'T CHANGE EURO PLAN   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia will not push forward its 2009 target for adopting the euro even if the European Union allows it to deduct the cost of pension reform from its fiscal deficit, Finance Minister Ivan Miklos said.   \par \par \uc2  FIRMING CROWN HELPS PUSH SLOVAK T-BOND YIELDS DOWN   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia saw the cost of state refinancing fall at an auction of state bonds on Monday as firming crown and shortage of new debt issues pushed yields on treasury bonds down.   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  AGAIN TO WEAKEN CROWN   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold crowns directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which had surged to a new record high to the euro.   \par \par \uc2  For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see . For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, dou