\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slovak crown holds near record peaks, zloty steady.  \b0\par\par\uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 12:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 1 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown remained firm on Tuesday in spite of signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking a tougher stance against its strength, with the Polish zloty also holding close to 2 1/2 year highs versus the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Strong foreign investment inflows continue to buoy the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it from the authorities.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell crowns again on Monday, after earlier cutting key interest rates by 100 basis points, but still weakened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  only a few pips from record highs against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "They're stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there's no question about that. We estimate that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February could have been as much as 1.8 billion euros, which is a massive amount in a market as small as this," said Koon Chow, emerging markets strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 It would also be a big leap after the bank said it bought 290 million euros in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January.  \par \par \uc2 "But I get the sense the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in a mindset to curb appreciation rather than trigger a reversal of the trend. I don't get a sense they're out to trigger stops or force a messy exit by trading desks," Chow added.  \par \par \uc2 By 1115 GMT, the crown traded at a bid price of 37.825 per euro , little changed on the session.  \par \par \uc2 The reformist credentials of the Slovak government have laid a platform for strong foreign investment inflows into the country.  \par \par \uc2 A growing number of foreign manufacturers are setting up plants in Slovakia and the government is hoping to seal a S.Korean investment project worth 500 million euros in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Chow said the one near-term risk factor was the size of long positions that have been built up in the crown, making the market vulnerable to a sharp decline in the event of an external shock.  \par \par \uc2 ZLOTY HOLDS FIRM  \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty remained within touching distance of 2 1/2-year highs against the euro, still finding support from a backdrop of a broadly soft dollar and low global interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The market shrugged off comments from the leader of Poland's main opposition Civic Platform party, Jan Rokita, that zloty strength is starting to become excessive.  \par \par \uc2 Rokita, whose party is well ahead in the polls in the run up to elections later this year, also said he would consider unilaterally adopting the euro as a means of preventing too much \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.  \par \par \uc2 "(Rokita's) are not too much to worry about. Certainly, the government is keeping an eye on zloty strength, but the rhetoric is mixed at moment," said Osman Wahid, emerging markets strategist at J.P.Morgan.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't want it to continue the sharp appreciation of the past 8 months, but you also have to consider that when euro/polish was at its highs most people thought the zloty was undervalued, so in that sense its been coming back into line."  \par \par \uc2 Wahid said the factors to watch out for a potential end to the zloty rally were analysts starting to cut back their growth forecasts and when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts cutting interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Council shifted its monetary policy bias to "easing" from "tightening" following its monthly meeting last Friday, but the move had little impact on the zloty.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty traded at 3.8960 to the euro  from 3.9011 and at 2.9445 to\par the dollar        from 2.9413.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Israeli shekel hits two-month highs against dollar, extending Monday's gains driven by companies converting dollars into shekels to pay salaries at the beginning of the month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The shekel was up 0.16 percent at 4.33 to the dollar .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050301e131009of\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
