\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on March 1.  \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, March 1 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK TO HOLD ITS REGULAR WEEKLY MEETING   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making Bank Board will hold its weekly meeting to decide on the result of the regular two-week repo tender.   \par \par \uc2  FIN MIN TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE ON TAX REFORM IMPACTS   \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Ivan Miklos will hold a news conference on the tax reform impacts.   \par \par \uc2  STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE JAN EU-NORM INFLATION DATA   \par \par \uc2  The statistics office will release January EU-norm inflation data.   \par \par \uc2  GOVT PRIVATISATION AGENCY TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE   \par \par \uc2  The National Property Fund, the government's privatisation agency, will hold a news conference on its 2005 plans.   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK CUTS INTEREST RATES TO REIN IN CROWN   \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its key two-week repo rate by 100 basis points to 3.0 percent on Monday to fight the continued firming of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  AGAIN TO WEAKEN CROWN   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had sold Slovak crowns in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the crown after it hit a record high of 37.810 per euro.   \par \par \uc2  C.BANK SAYS BOUGHT 290 MLN EUROS IN JAN   \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) bought 290 million euros ($386 million) through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January aimed at curbing firming pressure on the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK C/A GAP RISES TO SKK 45.2 BLN IN 2004   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's current account showed a deficit of 45.2 billion crowns ($1.6 billion) last year, compared with a 10.2 billion crown shortfall in 2003.   \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK JAN PPI DATA BEAT FCASTS   \par \par \uc2  Slovak producer prices fell by 0.2 percent on a monthly basis in January, putting annual price growth at 2.8 percent.   \par \par \uc2  SKYEUROPE EXPANDS FLEET, OPENS NEW ROUTES   \par \par \uc2  Slovak-based low cost airline SkyEurope will add four jet planes to its fleet for the summer season this year.   \par \par \uc2  For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see . For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click   \par \par \uc2  , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.   \par \par \uc2  News editor of the day: Martin Dokoupil on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2  E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com   \par \par \uc2  Reuters Messaging: martin.dokoupil.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\p