\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to weaken crown.   \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2005\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, extending its lengthy battle with investors who are pushing the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to record highs.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market on Friday when the crown hit 37.820 to the euro, its strongest level ever.   \par \par \uc2 The move was the fourth direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, and occurred just ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 NBS spokesman Igor Barat gave no details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers said the bank has been using foreign players to sell crowns to confuse the local market.   \par \par \uc2 "It looked like an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we were not sure because the NBS appeared to be going through a foreign bank," one Bratislava-based dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 The crown weakened only slightly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , moving to 37.870 to the euro.   \par \par \uc2 The crown has gained 2.3 percent against the euro this year, boosted by Slovakia's encouraging economic performance and expectations of strong foreign investment inflows.   \par \par \uc2 But the NBS considers the firming pace too fast and dangerous for the economy. Central bankers have also said their aim was to avoid a shock correction in the longer term as that could threaten fulfilment of euro adoption criteria.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fight against crown firming has sparked market talk about an interest rate cut at the February monetary policy meeting.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts are expecting a cut of as much as 100 basis points, after the NBS slashed two full percentage points off the main two-week repo rate last year to make the crown less attractive for speculators. The two-week repo is now 4.0 percent.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050225e12p00dnr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
