\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown ends firmer despite cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2005\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par ended within sight of its new highs of 37.835 to the euro on\par Thursday as the market fought off the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's attempt to\par dent crown buying sentiment with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  entered the market on Thursday for the\par third time this week to knock the crown off its record levels,\par but traders said its move was modest compared with the previous\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sold crowns\par directly on the market, but pushed the crown only up to 37.890\par (per euro)," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Vladimir Gajdos.\par     Traders said the crown picked up steam again as soon as the\par monetary body left the market, closing at 37.823/872 versus the\par euro, compared with 37.866/916 late on Wednesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The crown has firmed 2.3 percent against the euro so far\par this year as foreign investors are flocking into the new EU\par member lured by improving economic fundamentals and expectations\par of strong FDI inflows.\par     Market watchers said demand for crowns was set to remain\par strong in the coming days, adding the unit could test 37.800 per\par euro on Friday.\par     Investors are awaiting the outcome of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par Monday monetary meeting with a majority of analysts expecting a\par policy loosening of 50-100 basis points.\par  \par     The key two-week repo rate stands at 4.00 percent after the\par bank cut 200 basis points last year to deter hot-money inflows.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1540 GMT --------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/euro at 37.823/872 vs 37.866/916 on Wednesday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/dollar at 28.662/712 vs 28.676/711  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr yield at 2.993/2.868 pct vs 3.071/2.871 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10-yr yield at 3.615/415 pct vs 3.626/426 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050224e12o00enz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
