\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Upside pressure on forint eases, Czechs eye rates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2005\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The strong upside pressure on Hungary's forint subsided on Thursday, though analysts said it could be a temporary lull, while Czech crown dealers awaited a key interest rate decision.  \par \par \uc2 The forint tracked back from near two-year highs hit against the euro earlier in the week, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some breathing space after it rose close to the upper limit of its trading bands, which comes in around 240 to the euro .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zsigmond Jarai said on Wednesday the bank would, if necessary, defend the bands, though he said it had no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market as long as the bands hold.  \par \par \uc2 "The key point is when you get closer to bottom of the bands you will see higher volatility. Today's move higher (in euro/forint) is part of that," said Martin Blum, head of emerging markets research at HVB in Vienna.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it signifies a change in the trading environment and the rate could move lower again."  \par \par \uc2 By 1015 GMT, the forint was a touch down on the session around 242.50 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Nobody is under the illusion that the band would be moved, but by the same token \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments that it has no problem with the forint trading in its current range means perceptions of the risk of it moving higher are limited," Blum added.  \par \par \uc2 Blum said as long as players did not perceive a risk of a sharp move back to 245, the trend would remain for the forint to strengthen towards the band limit.  \par \par \uc2 The forint trades in ERM2-style bands allowing 15 percent fluctuations on either side of a central parity rate against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The Czech crown was little moved around 29.90 per euro ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly interest rate decision. Most analysts expect rates to be left on hold, but the market was wary following January's surprise cut to 2.25 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Our bias is against a cut. New board members will want to become more familiar with the data, and the bank may also see some scope for euro/czech to move higher on political uncertainty," said Blum at HVB.  \par \par \uc2 Three new board members will sit on the seven-member panel.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Stanislav Gross on Thursday called on President Vaclav Klaus to step into talks to resolve an excalating row within the ruling centre-left coalition, which threatens to cost the government its majority in parliament.  \par \par \uc2 The junior coalition partner, the Christian Democrats, have called on the Social Democrats to replace Gross due to questions about his personal finances.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Slovak crown traded at 37.84 to the euro , a fresh record high against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third time this week on Thursday, but did little more than hold up the crown's progress.  \par \par \uc2 LIRA UP ON IMF HOPES  \par \par \uc2 The new Turkish lira strengthened to under 1.3 per dollar , its best levels in 2-1/2 years, helped in part by comments from Finance Minister Kemal Unakitan on Wednesday that three key reform bills would be submitted to parliament over the next few days.  \par \par \uc2 Passage of the bills on social security, tax and banking are a pre-condition for the International Monetary Fund board approving a new $10 billion loan package to replace the $19 billion deal that expired this month.  \par \par \uc2 "Saying the social security bill would be forwarded next week is a step in the right direction," said Debbie Orgill, emerging markets analyst at ABN AMRO.  \par \par \uc2 "That's the biggest of the three because it would mean a big improvement for the fiscal outlook." The lira traded at 1.2960 to the dollar on the interbank market from 1.303 at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Orgill said the market would be wary of the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap lira gains under the 1.3 per dollar handle, especially with the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rising against the euro - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trading partner.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050224e12o0091a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
