\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Feb 24.  \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2005\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 BUSH MEETS PUTIN IN BRATISLAVA  \par \par \uc2 U.S. President George W. Bush and Russian President Vladimir Putin will hold one day summit in Bratislava.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  AGAIN TO REIN IN CROWN  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its long-lasting battle against the sharp firming of the crown on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high of 37.870 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 FIN MIN SCRAPS EUROBOND ISSUE PLAN  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia has scrapped a plan to issue a eurobond this year and will take advantage of low domestic interest rates to refinance its maturing debt, Deputy Finance Minister Vladimir Tvaroska said.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. STEEL KOSICE TO BUILD NEW $160 MLN LINE  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit of U.S. Steel (X.N) said on Wednesday it would invest $160 million to build a new production line to make coated steel and serve growing demand in the car and construction sectors in central Europe.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA EYES EUR 500 MLN PLANT BY FINNS  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia is in talks with Finnish paper maker Myllykoski, which is looking for a location to build a 500 million euro pulp processing plant in the central Europe.  \par \par \uc2 TREND page 52  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see . For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a ca