\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown at new high despite cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2005\par 19:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par firmed to settle beyond the long-resisting level of 38.0 per\par euro on Wednesday despite continued the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's attempts\par to slow the rise with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     The crown set off stronger on Wednesday after crossing the\par psychological mark late on Tuesday, but its quick move to 37.870\par per euro prompted a new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's action, the second this\par week, pushed the crown as far as 37.950 per euro, but the unit\par rebounded quickly to hit a new all-time high of 37.850.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action was triggered by the crown's\par firming pace. If they had not acted this morning we might have\par attacked 37.800 (per euro) or perhaps 37.750 now," said ING Bank\par dealer Jan Rafaj.\par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost part of its gains later in the\par session as foreign investors closed some of their positions to\par take profits. It closed at 37.866/916 to the euro, after\par 37.950/990 late on Tuesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected firming pressure on the crown to persist in\par the coming days, but added room for further gains would be\par limited by a risk of another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action.\par     Investors will now eye the outcome of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par monthly monetary meeting on Feb 28, but the market is split\par whether the bank decides to trim interest rates. Some predict as\par much as 100 basis points in policy easing on Monday.\par     The NBS last cut the key two-week repo rate in November,\par reducing it by 50 basis points to 4.0 percent to stem rapid rise\par of the crown.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1725 GMT --------------------\par Crown/euro  at 37.866/916 vs 38.950/990 on Tuesday\par Crown/dollar  at 28.676/711 vs 28.671/721\par 5-yr yield  at 3.071/2.871 pct vs 3.062/2.813 pct\par 10-yr yield  at 3.626/426 pct vs 3.607/452 pct\par ----------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050223e12n00dfl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
