\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Feb 22.  \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2005\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK BOARD MEETS TO DECIDE ON REPO RESULT  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making Bank Board will hold its weekly meeting to decide on the result of the regular two-week repo tender. The bank rejected all bids in the previous three auctions to stem firming pressure on the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK KEEPS FIGHTING CROWN WITH \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to combat the rapid rise of the crown on Monday by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from crossing the psychological 38.0 per euro level.  \par \par \uc2 GOVT BONDS DRAW HIGH DEMAND IN LIQUIDITY SURPLUS  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's sale of 10-year, 4.90 percent treasury bonds drew high demand on Monday as banks were flooded with excess funds and foreign investors kept betting on further firming of the crown. The state's debt and liquidity agency said it had sold 2.810 billion crowns ($96.4 million) worth of the paper in a tap auction. Bids totalled 11.985 billion crowns, down from a record 19.9 billion in the sale of five-year bonds earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see . For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050222e12m00829\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
