\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Forint dips further after rate cut.  \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2005\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint added to earlier losses on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by a larger than expected 75 basis points while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown.  \par \par \uc2 Hungary's Monetary Council said a favourable inflation outlook had allowed them to lower key rates to 8.25 percent, but added it would toe a cautious line going forward given the country's sizeable current account and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 The forint fell as low as 243.85 after the decision, but by 1454 GMT had recovered somewhat to trade around 243.40 per euro .  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts had expected the bank to cut by 50 basis points, but said surprisingly benign January inflation data and last week's forint strength had probably tipped the scales in favour of a bigger move.  \par \par \uc2 Some said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be disappointed if it hoped that in moving more aggressively it would help take some of the steam out of the forint's rally - it struck near two-year highs against the euro last week.  \par \par \uc2 "You can read it in two ways. A big easing now may persuade people to reduce long positions, on other hand you could take it as very bullish for bonds," said Zsolt Papp, emerging markets analyst at ABN AMRO.  \par \par \uc2 "The market might be inclined to go for the second reading."  \par \par \uc2 Foreign inflows into the bond market have driven the forint higher in recent weeks as investors bet on an accelerating pace of rate cuts boosting prices.  \par \par \uc2 Four new Monetary Council members, hand-picked by Prime Minister Ferenc Gyurcsany, are expected to give the rate-setting body a more dovish bias in future meetings.  \par \par \uc2 The forint is not far off the strong limit of its trading bands against the euro, which comes in around 240, though Governor Zsigmond Jarai said on Monday he was not concerned.  \par \par \uc2 The market was awash with rumours last week of sizeable positions being taken in the options market betting that the limit would be breached.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SLOVAK\b0 \highlight\uc2  CROWN DOWN AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown on Monday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier risen to a fresh record high of 37.95 per euro , in its fourth market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "We are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we are still not satisfied with the pace of the crown firming," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said with foreign investment inflows continuing to pour into the country, the best the bank could hope for was to hold the crown steady.  \par \par \uc2 "Including today, they've probably now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of over $1 bln in recent weeks, and only succeeded in keeping the crown flat," said Koon Chow, emerging markets strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown traded a shade down at 38.03 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 It was a less bullish picture for the neighbouring Czech crown, which retreated from 2 1/2 year highs against the euro as the pressure was cranked up on Prime Minister Stanislav Gross to resign. Gross vowed to fight on after a weekend meeting with President Vaclav Klaus following calls for him to quit from junior coalition partners, the Christian Democrats, over questions about the funding of his flat and his wife's business.  \par \par \uc2 The crown eased off its highs, but losses were fairly limited. It was down 0.2 percent to the euro at 29.91 .  \par \par \uc2 If the Christian Democrats leave the coalition, the government would lose its one-vote parliamentary majority, though analysts said they would probably not want to trigger early elections.  \par \par \uc2 Shares in the country's leading phone company Cesky Telecom (SPTTsp.PR) dipped on concerns the political spat was a threat to the firm's upcoming $3 billion privatisation.  \par \par \uc2 The crown's strong gains so far this year have, in part, been built on expectations of strong foreign inflows arising from the Cesky sale.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050221e12l00el6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
