\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to soften crown.   \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2005\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to combat the rapid rise of the crown on Monday by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from crossing the psychological 38.0 per euro level.   \par \par \uc2 The direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the fourth such a move in the past two weeks and started shortly after the crown hit a record high of 37.950 per euro, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "We are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because we are still not satisfied with the pace of the crown firming," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters. The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) has been crossing swords with speculators for more than a year to correct what it calls excessive exchange rate swings, saying such movements were damaging for the economy.   \par \par \uc2 The monetary body has been criticsed by analysts and international institutions such as International Monetary Fund for managing the exchange rate too tightly on its way to achieve inflation criteria needed to adopt the euro.   \par \par \uc2 But the bank has said that it had to fight too strong a firming pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a potential sharp correction in the future.   \par \par \uc2 Barat said the NBS was ready to use all instruments to prevent exchange rate moves, which were unjustified by economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit retreated as far as 38.095 to the euro following the NBS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It traded at 38.033/083 per euro at 1215 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also used liquidity-draining repo tenders in recent weeks to push interbank deposit rates down and thus eliminate firming pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is evidently defending the 38.0 per euro level and probably will not change its strategy until the new inflation figures are released," one dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 But traders said the NBS tactics would have only temporary impact on the crown, adding investors' would keep pushing the unit stronger in the coming days amid positive sentiment on the neighbouring markets.   \par \par \uc2 The crown has firmed 1.8 percent against the euro this year, helped by Slovakia's improving economic performance and expectations of strong investment inflows from abroad.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the NBS bought roughly 200 million euros in Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The market expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates again this month or in March to keep the crown in check.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS trimmed borrowing costs by 200 basis points last year, bringing the key two-week repo rate to 4.0 percent, but later switched to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the rate reductions failed to temper the market's bullish mood.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050221e12l00btd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
