\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Feb 11.  \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2005\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE DEC FOREIGN TRADE DATA  \par \par \uc2 The statistics office will release December foreign trade data.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK TO RELEASE WEEKLY \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DATA  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release its weekly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO FIGHT CROWN STRENGTH  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) resumed its lengthy battle against the steep climb of the crown, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to soften the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it matched recent all-time highs versus the euro.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK JAN CPI SLOWS, SPARKS TALKS OF RATE CUT  \par \par \uc2 Slovak headline inflation slowed down for a sixth month running in January, and analysts said the favourable trend could open the door for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to loosen monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 Headline inflation was 1.7 percent month-on-month in January, putting the annual rate at 3.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 ORANGE SLOVAKIA SALES UP 18 PCT Y/Y IN 2004  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's largest cell phone operator Orange (OGE.L) (FTE.PA) said on Thursday its sales rose by 18 percent to 19.2 billion crowns ($644.5 million) in 2004, fuelled by continued inflow of new customers.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK PM SAYS U.S.-RUSSIA SUMMIT TO CROWN REFORMS  \par \par \uc2 Slovak Prime Minister Mikulas Dzurinda said on Thursday a summit between U.S. and Russian leaders in Slovakia this month would crown transformation of a one-time European pariah into a mainstream Western country.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA EXPECTS FDI INFLOWS TO CONTINUE IN FUTURE  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak government investment agency SARIO said inflows of foreign direct investments (FDI) were likely to keep growing in the next three to four years due to Slovakia's attractive business environment.  \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny page 5  \par \par \uc2 SKYEUROPE TO SPEND UP TO 30 MLN EUROS IN 2005  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's low-cost airline SkyEurope plans to spend 10-30 million euros this year, mainly to expand its network, strengthen its balance sheet and for leasing deposits for new airplanes. The upstart carrier aims to invest further 50-70 million to its fleet expansion and cost-cutting measures in the future.  \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny page 13  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see . For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emergin