\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to curb crown strength.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil   \par \uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2005\par 16:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 10 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) resumed its battle against the strengthening crown on Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market for the second time this week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matched recent all-time highs versus the euro.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS has been trying to slow what it sees as unjustified crown appreciation for more than a year, saying it could damage the economy and endanger euro adoption later this decade.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown twice on Thursday, first using covert deals with London-based banks when the unit touched a record high of 38.000 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 It stepped into the market again when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded to 38.030 per euro from 38.100.   \par \par \uc2 "I can confirm we have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was motivated by the NBS's ongoing dissatisfaction with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  developments which are harmful to the economy," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 He said the bank would keep watching the crown moves and was ready to use all available tools to correct unwarranted exchange rate swings in the future, echoing the NBS's recent comments.   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit retreated back towards the 38.100 per euro level following the second round of the NBS action. It traded at 38.048/098 per euro at 1525 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 The bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market four times this year to keep the crown in check. It has also left the money market in a huge liquidity surplus in the past week to deter inflows of short-term capital.   \par \par \uc2 The crown, which is up 1.7 percent against the euro this year, has been rising rapidly over recent months boosted by Slovakia's improving economic performance, expectations of foreign direct investment and debt rating upgrades.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS has said it is not against gradual crown firming based on improving productivity, but has warned the market that it would carry on its crusade against the unit's rally if it is not in line with economic trends.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS board used hefty rate cuts last year to make the crown less attractive for speculators, but has indicated recently that it would stick to other tools as the unit's rise seemed to be no longer driven by interest differentials.   \par \par \uc2 However, analysts said that positive January inflation figures, released earlier on Thursday, created room for the bank to bring the key two-week repo rate, which stands at 4.0 percent, down further to ease firming pressure on the crown.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS trimmed credit costs by 200 basis points last year despite analysts' warnings that such a policy loosening might trigger demand-led inflationary pressures in the future.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the bank's latest action would soften the crown only temporarily as weaker levels usually trigger more crown buying, adding players would keep testing its determination to defend the psychological 38.0 per euro level in the coming days.   \par \par \uc2 "They (the NBS) will not reverse the firming trend... they can only slow it down temporarily," said ING Bank dealer Jan Rafaj. The NBS was estimated to have bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth roughly 200 million euros in Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared with around 400 million on Monday.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050210e12a00cnm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
