\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown flat after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , mkt eyes repo.  \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2005\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 8 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown           was\par steady on Tuesday after Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par halted its rise, with dealers awaiting the result of a repo\par tender.\par     The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday for\par the second time in less than a week and the third time this\par year, saying the crown's rise was too fast and harmful for the\par economy.\par     The NBS stepped into the market when the unit threatened to\par break 38.000 per euro on Monday, and traders said that level\par could now stand as a psychological resistance for short-term\par players in the near term.\par     However, most traders said they expected new attempts to\par break the 38.0 level in the coming days as foreign investors\par remained bullish on the Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the central European\par region in general.\par  \par     "I see it going slowly down (the crown firming). The trend\par has not changed," said ING Bank trader Jan Rafaj.\par     The next market moving impulse could come from a regular\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repo tender on Tuesday. The bank rejected all bids  \par \par \uc2 in the two-week repo last week, leaving the market in a large  \par \par \uc2 liquidity surplus in an attempt to discourage speculators.  \par \par \uc2 But the repo decision failed to weaken the crown as most of  \par \par \uc2 foreign funds are not attracted by short-term interest rates but  \par \par \uc2 by the prospect of future crown gains.  \par \par \uc2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1600 GMT -  \par \par \uc2 Crown/euro at 38.065/085 vs 38.070/090 on Monday  \par \par \uc2 Crown/dollar at 29.777/827 vs 29.660/695  \par \par \uc2 5-yr yield at 3.200/2.900 pct vs 3.141/2.941 pct  \par \par \uc2 10-yr yield at 3.799/599 pct vs 3.796/638 pct  \par \par \uc2 -.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050208e128008sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
