\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown drops on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , seen up again.  \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2005\par 17:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par weakened on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in\par the market to halt the unit's rise, but dealers said they\par expected more upward pressure in the near future.\par     The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) sold crowns for the\par second time in less than a week and for the third time this\par year, stepping into the market when the unit approached its\par all-time high of 38.000 to the euro.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as low as 38.150\par per euro, but local exporters and foreign players quickly jumped\par on the cheaper crown and pushed it back to stronger levels.\par     "Nothing has changed. The barrier on the upper (weak) side\par is 38.200, and the NBS is the only thing holding the crown back\par on the other side," said HVB Bank dealer Marian Sulko.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The NBS has been slowing crown appreciation for more than a\par year with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rate cuts and liquidity tools, saying\par that fast appreciation would hurt the economy and could threaten\par the plan to meet euro adoption criteria in 2007.\par     Dealers said they expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep\par preventing the crown from firming through the psychological\par level of 38.000 per euro for some time, but they predicted new\par attacks on the mark in the coming days.\par  \par     "I think it is now only a question of time when the crown\par moves beyond 38.0," Sulko said.\par     Prospects of future crown gains and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attempt\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to rein in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by flooding the market with liquidity  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 have attracted strong demand in an auction of five-year state  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bonds on Monday and cut the state's refinancing costs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will watch the result of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday, after the NBS rejected  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 all bids in last week's repo and left the market with a large  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 liquidity surplus.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1600 GMT -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/euro at 38.070/090 vs 38.020/040 on Friday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/dollar at 29.660/695 vs 29.330/350  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr yield at 3.141/2.941 pct vs 3.212/2.964 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10-yr yield at 3.796/638 pct vs 3.790/610 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050207e12700h1x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
