\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty uneasy after Hausner quits, Slovaks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2005\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty tripped up from two year highs against the euro on Monday after Economy Minister Jerzy Hausner quit the ruling party.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown's rally also paused following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it this year, while the South African rand and Turkish lira awaited key interest rate decisions later in the week.  \par \par \uc2 The zloty extended its recent upward charge early on, setting new peaks around 3.9520 before Hausner's departure triggered a bout of profit taking.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Hausner's decision to leave the leftist Democratic Left Alliance, after the party tamed his plans to control public spending, could knock the firming zloty in the short-term if he forms another party to contest the elections.  \par \par \uc2 "If a new party did form in the coming months and that did have some participation from present government members that could disturb the zloty," HVB analyst Martin Blum said.  \par \par \uc2 By 1125 GMT, the zloty was down 0.16 percent at 3.97, but still close to 25-month highs .  \par \par \uc2 Government officials said Hausner should resign from the cabinet and he has said he may work with a new movement potentially involving Prime Minister Marek Belka.  \par \par \uc2 Polls predict the ruling party could lose elections this year.  \par \par \uc2 However, a new reform-based centrist party could ease external concerns about the influence of extreme political parties ahead of this year's elections and boost the zloty.  \par \par \uc2 "It could reduce the level of support for some of the more activist parties which would reduce election risks," Blum said.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\uc2  AGAIN  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulling the crown back from the 38.00 per euro barrier, would not have much long-term impact because of continued strong investment flows.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has attempted to stem the crown's rise out of fear that a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hurt exports. The bank last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "The response of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown to this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been very shallow," Credit Suisse First Boston strategist Koon Chow said. "We have a constructive medium term view on the crown."  \par \par \uc2 The crown was down 0.17 percent to 38.06 per euro , off of all-time highs set last week.  \par \par \uc2 However, Chow said investors looking for positive economic data similar to that in the Czech Republic last week could be caught out.  \par \par \uc2 "My one nagging concern is that investors may have a very positive expectation of trade data out this Friday and there could be scope for disappointment," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Czech crown continued to rise, equalling Friday's 2-1/2 year highs at 29.90 per euro .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the South African rand's slide against the dollar bucked the trend among other commodity producers.  \par \par \uc2 "People are increasingly concerned about the rand which may increase ahead of the Monetary Policy Council meeting this week," Chow said.  \par \par \uc2 Opinion is divided on the direction of Thursday's policy meeting. Some analysts expect rates to stay at 7.5 percent but others have not ruled out a cut.  \par \par \uc2 The rand was down a touch against the dollar at 6.14 .  \par \par \uc2 The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also decide the direction of monetary policy this week, with some analysts expecting another 100 basis point cut from the meeting slated for Tuesday and Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight borrowing rate is currently 17 percent and the overnight lending rate is 21 percent. The lira held firm at 1.3145 per dollar in interbank trade .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050207e12700c1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
