\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown seen testing  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level.  \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2005\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown was steady\par near its all-time highs early on Friday, but dealers said the\par market looked set to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stronger levels again\par and provoke a new round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) sold crowns directly on\par the market on Thursday for the second time this year, starting\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the unit reached the psychological level\par of 38.000 per euro.\par  \par     The crown firmed alongside other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in central\par Europe as London players boosted their exposure in the region.\par     "It's only a matter of time when we move through 38.0 (per\par euro)," said Tatra Banka trader Boris Somorovsky.\par     "I would expect NBS to act again when the crown goes to\par 38.0, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should not push the crown higher\par (weaker) than around 38.200," he added.\par     The NBS has been trying to slow crown appreciation for more\par than a year, saying the unit's sharp rise was harmful for the\par economy.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The crown has jumped by 1.8 percent since the start of the\par year as investors expect future strengthening on the back of\par solid economic growth and inflows of foreign direct investments.\par     Traders said interest in crown purchases among foreign banks\par was likely to last in the coming days, adding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par will have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regularly to slow the unit's rise.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0830 GMT --------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Crown/euro  at 38.045/055 vs 38.015/030 on Thursday\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Crown/dollar  at 29.300/340 vs 29.320/350\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5-yr yield  at 3.091/2.911 pct vs 3.090/2.910 pct\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-yr yield  at 3.820/640 pct vs 3.833/633 pct\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050204e124008kj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
