\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown near highs despite cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2005\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown closed near\par all-time highs on Thursday despite direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  designed to halt the unit's rise, dealers said.\par     After repeated verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 stepped into the market and sold crowns when the unit reached  \f28 \par \par \uc2 the psychological level of 38.000 per euro, its strongest rate  \par \par \uc2 ever versus the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) repeated its view that  \par \par \uc2 the recent crown firming - a 1.8 percent jump since the start of  \par \par \uc2 the year - was not justified by economic fundamentals and was  \par \par \uc2 harmful for the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which traders estimated the NBS to have  \par \par \uc2 bought 100-150 million euros, briefly pushed the crown to around  \par \par \uc2 38.200 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But many traders used the opportunity to buy cheaper crowns\par and the unit resumed firming again in afternoon activity.\par     "The (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) showed that it does not want to see the\par crown below 38.000, so it could hold as a barrier for some\par time," said VUB Bank trader Laco Benedek.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been trying to slow crown appreciation\par for over a year, using direct and secret \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rate\par cuts and liquidity management tools.\par     Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seemed to be the most effective\par tool to manage crown appreciation, and they said the NBS would\par have to step into the market regularly to slow the unit's rise.\par     "I expect that mainly London players will continue trying to\par push the crown through 38.0 again," Benedek said.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1600 GMT --------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/euro at 38.015/030 vs 38.044/094 on Wednesday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/dollar at 29.320/350 vs 29.240/280  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr yield at 3.090/2.910 pct vs 3.259/057 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10-yr yield at 3.833/633 pct vs 3.884/684 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050203e12300dtk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
