.200 per euro, but traders, mainly foreign banks, used the move to buy cheaper crowns again.   \par \par \uc2 "The market seems to be calming down at the moment. I would expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do the same (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) if the crown moves to 38.0 again in the afternoon," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Vladimir Gajdos.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050203e123009ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
