\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty leads C.Europe higher, hits 25-month highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2005\par 11:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 3 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit new highs on Thursday, led by the Polish zloty which scaled 25-month peaks against the euro on talk of strong foreign demand.  \par \par \uc2 A fresh bout of zloty strength began on Wednesday after Economy Minister Jerzy Hausner signalled there was little he could do to stop it rising further.  \par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended gains under the four-per-euro level on Thursday, with dealers reporting a combination of option-related and hedge fund buying.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been some interest from hedge funds. On one level people have been hedging options positions, while those who trade the zloty on a technical basis will have been brought in by a strong close last night," said one London analyst.  \par \par \uc2 One dealer said the market had knocked out key options-related levels between 4.05-4.00, triggering automatic euro sell orders.  \par \par \uc2 "With the dollar rangebound elsewhere, the big hedge funds are keen to put their money to work in high yield emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in particular the zloty, Brazilian real and Mexican peso," the analyst said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 1007 GMT, the zloty traded at 3.9908 to the euro  from 4.0674 late\par on Wednesday and at 3.0648 to the dollar        from 3.1095.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As widely expected, the U.S. Federal Reserve lifted key U.S. interest rates by 25 basis points to 2.5 percent, but kept to its line that monetary policy would be tightened at a measured pace.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the Fed move would do little to erode the attractiveness of high yield \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the focus now shifting to Friday's U.S. jobs report for the latest clue on the rate outlook.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Signs of a more dovish rate outlook in Poland were said to inspire strong demand at a domestic bond auction on Wednesday, further buoying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Demand at the bond auction was more locally driven, with the speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is moving to more expansionary monetary policy stance providing support to the bond market," said Caio Natividade, emerging markets strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natividade added that yield erosion was unlikely to become a factor undermining the zloty anytime soon, with interest rates not seen coming down until the second half of the year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint tracked zloty gains to hit its best levels against the euro in two months around 244 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH, SLOVAK CROWNS BUOYANT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The soaring run enjoyed by the Czech and Slovak crowns so far this year extended on Thursday, with the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  setting its best levels since September 2002 under 30 per euro and the Slovak hitting record highs around 38 per euro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strong foreign investment inflows, rather than high yields, have been the driving force behind the rallies in both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , though the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action to guard against excessive strength is ever present in both.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Slovak Finance Minister Ivan Miklos said on Wednesday the crown rise was dangerous for the economy, underlining the risk of further crown-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Strong economic and fiscal fundamentals, coupled with highly positive market sentiment towards the region should sustain the appreciation pressure," said analysts at BNP Paribas in a research note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We expect, however, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in with direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  once euro/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown breaks below 38.0."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown was a touch firmer at 38.03 per euro , with the Czech crown at 29.99 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050203e1230089p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
