\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Markets becalmed pre-Fed, Slovak crown nudges down.  \b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2005\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were broadly calm on Wednesday awaiting the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve monetary policy meeting later on, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown dipped on wariness over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A further 25 basis point hike from the Fed is seen as fully priced in, with focus likely to be on the accompanying statement for any sign of a shift in the measured pace of tightening stance.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone is expecting a 25 basis point hike, it's the language that really matters and there's nothing to suggest a shift away from this measured pace," said Dwyfor Evans, emerging markets analyst at Bank of America.  \par \par \uc2 "If that's the case, it's unlikely to have any impact on the high yielders, they should be able to carry on plugging away strongly."  \par \par \uc2 Euro/dollar nudged firmer ahead of the decision, expected at 1915 GMT, lending some support to the South African rand which tends to track the rate closely.  \par \par \uc2 By 1054 GMT, the rand was bid at 6.01 per dollar , off intra-day peaks around 5.9825.  \par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira edged up, continuing its strong run following the European Union's decision late last year to allow Turkey to begin entry negotiations in October.  \par \par \uc2 Underlining Turkey's increasing attractiveness, a consultant to Calpers, the biggest U.S. pension fund, said on Wednesday Turkey was now eligible to join the fund's list of emerging markets for investment.  \par \par \uc2 The lira traded at 1.3265 to the dollar on the interbank market , from 1.3275 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK CROWN DIPS  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown eased off record highs against the euro with the market wary of the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly on Tuesday by flooding the repo market with crown liquidity. It rejected all bids totalling 116.107 billion crowns at a weekly repo tender.  \par \par \uc2 "It's another signal they're opposed to rapid appreciation of the crown and people are perhaps also taking a breather with the market approaching a round number (38 per euro)," said Lucy Bethell, emerging markets analyst at Royal Bank of Scotland.  \par \par \uc2 The crown was marginally down at 38.09 per euro .  \par \par \uc2 Bethell added investors would still be happy to sell into euro rallies on the view the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only really slow the pace of gains. Foreign investment inflows into the country also show no sign of slowing.  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia earlier this week announced plans to offer incentives to a Ford Motor Co. (F.N) venture to invest 345 million euros on a new gearbox plant in the country and also hopes to attract 500 million euros worth of fresh investment from South Korea.  \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty showed little negative reaction to the likely scolding Poland will receive from the European Commission later today for insufficient progress on fiscal reform.  \par \par \uc2 In an assessment of Poland's "convergence plan", obtained by Reuters on Tuesday, the EU executive will say the country is unlikely to reach its target of lowering the budget gap below the EU's three percent of GDP limit in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 "Despite the criticisms of (Economy Minister Jerzy) Hausner's fiscal reform plans, he has still got a lot through," said Evans at BoA.  \par \par \uc2 "I'd say Poland is still a low level risk. There should be a sufficient level of reform done by the new government, and fiscal revenues should be pretty robust."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty traded at 4.0518 to the euro  from 4.0508 and at 3.1030 to\par the dollar        from 3.1115.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050202e12200ci2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
