\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Jan 19.  \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2005\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT HOLDS REGULAR MEETING  \par \par \uc2 The government will hold its regular weekly meeting. Ministers are expected to debate the country's recent arbitration loss to a Czech unit of KBC bank (KBKBt.BR).  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK SIGNALS MAY FAVOUR CROWN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) signalled on Tuesday it is likely to use direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than interest rate cuts to stem the pace of crown firming and keep the country's euro adoption goal on track.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK ACCEPTS ALL BIDS IN 2-WK REPO  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accepted all bids in its regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday, draining 107.188 billion crowns ($3.6 billion) of surplus liquidity from the market.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK JOBLESS RATE RISES IN DEC  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's unemployment rate rose to 13.07 percent in December 2004, from November's 12.58 percent in the first monthly increase after 10 consecutive declines.  \par \par \uc2 SE TO RETURN STATE GUARANTEES WORTH EUR 500 MLN  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's dominant power firm Slovenske Elektrarne (SE) will return state guarantees for loans worth 500 million euros by mid-May, following its recent debt restructuring. The state guarantees for credit worth 200-250 million euros will remain in place. The debt-ridden utility is expected to be taken over by Italy's Enel (ENEI.MI) later this year.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda page 12  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050119e11j0093u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
