\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank signals may favour crown  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca  \par \uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2005\par 17:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 18 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) signalled on Tuesday it is likely to use direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than interest rate cuts to stem the pace of crown firming and keep the country's euro adoption goal on track.  \par \par \uc2 The NBS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to slow the crown's rise to record highs against the euro. It has also slashed interest rates in its fight to deter speculative capital.  \par \par \uc2 But NBS Vice-Governor Elena Kohutikova told a meeting of corporate leaders that the country's higher interest rates compared with major markets were no longer the driving factor for the crown, with inflows now attracted by expectations of future crown firming.  \par \par \uc2 "We are reacting to exchange rate developments and we will continue reacting in the future," Kohutikova said.  \par \par \uc2 "We are not against a gradual appreciation, but we are against a scenario that the exchange rate is defined by short term capital rather than the economy."  \par \par \uc2 The crown closed at 38.630/680 versus the euro , its main reference unit, on Tuesday, a touch weaker than the 38.500 level where the NBS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, buying euros to flood the market with crowns.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is beginning to feel that (crown firming) is not about interest rate differential and this suggests that it would prefer \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than rate cuts to influence the crown," said ING Bank Chief Economist Jan Toth.  \par \par \uc2 Toth added he expected the crown to firm at a slower pace than in 2004, predicting a four percent rise this year after a six percent jump last year.  \par \par \uc2 Several economists have criticised the NBS for managing the exchange rate too tightly at the time when its monetary policy switched to inflation targeting as of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 But Kohutikova said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy was designed to ensure the smooth fulfilment of euro adoption criteria.  \par \par \uc2 "We want the exchange rate to develop in a way that can be backed up by the economy so that it does not bring danger to inflation criterion as well as the ERM-2 (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuation) criterion," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak convergence programme expects the country to meet all euro adoption criteria by end-2007 so the new EU member can adopt the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at start of 2009.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050118e11i00j7v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
