\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  against crown if CPI good.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca  \par \uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2005\par 17:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 17 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it may use \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the crown's rise if such action did not endanger its inflation goal, and analysts said the warning signalled a continued fight against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming.  \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past year to slow the crown's rise to record highs against the euro, sparked by an outlook for strong investment inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Several economists have criticised the NBS for managing the exchange rate too tightly at the time when its monetary policy switched to inflation targeting as of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 But NBS board member Martin Barto dismissed such criticism of policy inconsistency in remarks to reporters in parliament.  \par \par \uc2 "You can use \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but you have to be sure that the subsequent monetary policy easing will not endanger your inflation target," Barto said.  \par \par \uc2 "And if the (inflation) development is even better than expectations, then there is no problem."  \par \par \uc2 The NBS has described the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise as too fast compared with improvement in economic fundamentals, such as productivity growth, and said that such a sharp firming may have hurt the economy in the longer term.  \par \par \uc2 Barto's remarks followed comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Ivan Sramko, who said last week the NBS would use all tools to counter unjustifiably quick crown firming. The latest comments signalled more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in the pipeline.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue, until a point where the NBS calculates that it could jeopardise its inflation goals," said CSOB Bank analyst Marek Gabris.  \par \par \uc2 PAUSE FOR RATE CUTS?  \par \par \uc2 In addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also cut interest rates by a total of 200 basis points last year to make the crown less attractive for speculators taking advantage of higher rates compared with major markets.  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia posted better than expected inflation data in December 2004, which some analysts said could provide an argument for more monetary policy easing if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to use the cost of money as a tool to curb crown rise.  \par \par \uc2 However, when asked if December inflation opened room for more interest rate cuts, Barto said: "We need to see what happens in the first months of this year. I would not draw major conclusions (from December data)."  \par \par \uc2 Data released on Friday showed a headline inflation rate of 5.9 percent in December, near the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 5.7-7.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown gained more than six percent to the euro last year despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts to halt the rise and hit a record high of 38.500 last week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 38.610/630 to the euro on Monday, only slightly weaker from Friday's 38.568/618.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market will become more sensitive when the crown moves close to its all time highs again because of fears of new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a majority of players expects the unit to appreciate throughout the year.  \par \par \uc2 "The market can now easier absorb \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  than one or two years ago. The NBS will have to act repeatedly to slow the (firming) trend," said Tatra Banka dealer Boris Somorovsky.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050117e11h00ecp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
