\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Focus On Czech Nov Indus Output  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2005\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par  \par 0900/0800 Hungary November Trade Deficit \par           Seen EUR260M vs EUR390M in Oct \par  \par 0900/0800 Hungary November Industrial Production \par  \par 1200/1100 Hungary Auctions 3-Month T-Bills \par  \par 1200/1100 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Two-Week Deposits Tender \par  \par  N/A/N/A  Czech Republic November Industrial Output \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous  % Chg   Daily   Daily   % Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/PLN 4.0730-92  4.0591-31  +0.34  4.0735  4.0561   -0.17 \par EUR/HUF 247.78-98  247.75-95  +0.01  247.90  247.60   +1.09 \par EUR/CZK 30.25-30   30.250-80   0.00  30.250  30.277   -0.49 \par EUR/SKK 38.691-41  38.693-43  -0.01  38.693  38.741   -0.06 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 POLISH ZLOTY: hints from Monetary Policy Council members that the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might drop its tightening bias within the next month is likely to keep pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says CSFB. Also, foreign investors' appetite for carry trades is diminishing and current positions are likely to be unwound, which won't help the zloty.  \par \par \uc2 The zloty opened higher Monday, as the dollar stabilized following last week's rally and investors sold euro/zloty and dollar/zloty. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost some ground against the dollar later in the day. The zloty closed at PLN4.070-.0752 to the euro, from PLN4.0920 Friday, and at PLN3.1120.-1243 to the dollar, from PLN3.1330.  \par \par \uc2 HUNGARIAN FORINT should weaken to HUF249.50-250.00 to the euro as the market continues to second guess how the new set-up at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Council will influence the next rate decision Jan. 24, according to CIBX. The prime minister nominated three new members Friday and the bank appointed a new vice president Monday. Goldman Sachs revised its rate cut forecast down to 75 basis points from 100 basis points as it considers that the Monetary Council is only likely to be expanded after the date of the next meeting. That doesn't change its view that the new members will force rates lower until the forint weakens.  \par \par \uc2 The forint had a good morning Monday on the back of a slide in the dollar, but weakened slightly in the afternoon to close at HUF247.64-248.14 to the euro, from HUF248.28 late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 THE CZECH KORUNA: resistance at CZK30.25 is expected to hold Tuesday, local traders say.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to CZK30.25-.33 to the euro Monday, from CZK30.335 late Friday, gaining on expectations of solid 13.7% industrial growth in November, ahead of the release of the data Tuesday. Gains for the zloty also supported the koruna, while the latter shrugged off news of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Slovakia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLISH BONDS are likely to be under pressure for the rest of the week. The PLN2.6 billion auction of 10-year bonds Wednesday, inflation data later this week and new bond issuance, which the government will use to cover Paris Club debt, will weigh on local bonds in the short term, says BRE Bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local bonds were mostly flat Monday, having traded in a narrow range despite news of new supply on Wednesday. The two-year bond yielded 6.17%, up from 6.15% Friday, while the five-year bond yield was unchanged at 6.35%. At the auction of PLN600 million of 52-week treasury bills, the average yield rose to 6.260% from 6.250% at the previous tender. The bid-to-cover ratio was 3.1, down from 4.9 previously.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARIAN BONDS: short maturities will be supported by the redemption of HUF115 billion of debt Wednesday, while the rest of the curve will take its cue from forint trading Tuesday, says CIBX.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local bond yields rose across the curve early Monday on profit-taking prompted by a weaker forint, but stabilized in late trade. The move was especially pronounced on the three-year paper, with the yield rising to 8.50% at one stage before closing at 8.38%, up from 8.31% Friday. The five-year paper yielded 8.05%, up seven basis points on the day.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH BONDS: trading this week will likely continue to focus on larger European markets, but market will also eye industrial output data for November, due Tuesday. Yields on the 10-year paper could test the 4% level, London traders say.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Czech bond yields were down slightly Monday, falling one to two basis points across the curve in line with Western European bonds. News that outstanding bond issues in the fourth quarter totaled CZK571.4 billion, down from CZK572.2 billion at the end of the previous quarter, was slightly supportive.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    1889.81   loss  12.98   dn 0.7% \par BUX                     14586.69   loss 139.47   dn 0.9% \par PX-D                     2638.8    loss   3.5    dn 0.1% \par  \par DJ STOXX EU Enlarged 15  1801.78   loss   1.84   dn 0.1% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW, the WIG20 is likely to recover as it is close to support levels, but traders expect the index could slide to 1700-1750 in a few months time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The WIG20 ended down 0.7% Monday as foreign funds continued to sell and local demand failed to match supply. The selling centered on three blue-chip stocks, according to a local broker: KGHM, which fell 2.8%, in part due to falling copper prices, PKN, down 0.3%, and bank PKO, down 2.1%. Bank Pekao shares were unchanged.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST, there is no technical level to stop MOL's decline and, if it continues to fall, the rest of the market will fall with it, according to local traders.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BUX closed down 0.9% on heavy profit taking, with MOL responsible for two thirds of all trading volume. A decline in MOL's refinery margins were the selling trigger Monday and the stock closed down 2.3%. Matav fell 2.5% and Richter 0.7% as investors realized profits. Egis closed up 0.3% despite heavy recent gains, while OTP was up 0.4%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE, the market is likely to rise Tuesday on signs of new capital inflows into the region, mostly from the U.S. funds, say local traders.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The PX-D closed down 0.1% Monday as blue chips in general corrected after gains last week. Erste Bank fell 1.4%, Unipetrol fell 0.6%, while Philip Morris Czech Republic and Komercni Banka closed down 0.3%. Profit-taking pushed Cesky Telecom down 0.1%. Only CEZ and Zentiva bucked the trend, closing up 1.5% and 0.1%, respectively. [ 01-11-05 0129ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OVERNIGHT NEWS \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Poland's forthcoming EUR1.5 billion eurobond issue will price to offer between 26 and 29 basis points over mid-market swaps, a market source said Monday. The bond carries a 15-year maturity and is being managed by BNP Paribas, Citigroup Inc., and Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian oil and gas company MOL Magyar Olaj- es Gazipari Rt. (MOL.BU) said Monday that it has made a second discovery of oil and gas in the Tal Block, located in the Northern Western Frontier Province of Pakistan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Vanya Dragomanovich; Dow Jones Newswires; 44 207 842 9487; vanya.dragomanovich@dowjones.com [ 01-11-05 0129ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020050111e11b00006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
