\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to slow crown.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil  \par \uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2005\par 17:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 10 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) on Monday continued its crusade against the record rise of the crown, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it hit record highs against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been fighting against what it sees as excessive crown appreciation for more than a year, saying it could hurt the new EU member's economy.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday the NBS showed its policy had not changed despite the Jan. 1 appointment of Ivan Sramko as the new governor.  \par \par \uc2 According to dealers the NBS started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown late in the session when it hit 38.510 per euro , and sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 38.750 per euro after it traded near record highs of 38.500 earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 "I can confirm we are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The reason remains the same - too rapid a firming of the crown, which is not in line with economic fundamentals," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit lost more than 0.5 percent to the euro following the NBS move to close at 38.696/746 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 The monetary body last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dent firming pressure on the crown in December when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped to 38.530 per euro following a two-month rally fuelled by encouraging economic data, expectations of large FDI inflows and a rating upgrade.  \par \par \uc2 Sramko took over stewardship of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Marian Jusko's six-year term ended on Dec. 31 pledging to continue to fight against a rapidly rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been firming rapidly over the past year, gaining more than six percent to the euro despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts to halt its rise with direct and off-market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hefty rate cuts and liquidity-draining tenders.  \par \par \uc2 The NBS has said it does not oppose gradual crown firming based on improving productivity, and it expects a stronger crown in the longer term, but it wanted to battle hot-money inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soften somewhat its stiff opposition to the strong crown this year after it said last month it would turn its focus to inflation-targeting from managing the exchange rate moves.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action would have only a temporary impact on the market's bullish mood as softer levels usually attract more crown buying.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still high demand for crowns, so we do not expect it to weaken significantly after this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said VUB Bank dealer Laco Benedek.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers expected the crown would probably settle above 38.600 per euro in the coming days, saying it was unlikely to retreat above a strongly defended level of 38.800 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 They said, however, the crown would probably resume firming in the coming weeks, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might try to curb its advance again if it nears its record highs too quickly.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 100-150 million euros in Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down from estimated 400-500 million in December.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050110e11a00hlo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
