\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Jan 3.  \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2005\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN TO RELEASE 2004 STATE BUDGET DATA  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry will release the central state budget data for full year 2004.  \par \par \uc2 NEW CBANK HEAD SAYS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  SUCCESSFUL  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ivan Sramko said on Saturday that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the sharp rise of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro were successful.  \par \par \uc2 He also told Reuters after being officially approved as the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor by the president that further actions to stem the crown's rise are on the cards if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms out of line with economic developments.  \par \par \uc2 SMK SEES OPPOSITION PARTIES IN NEXT GOVT  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's next government after the 2006 elections will probably include one of the currently strongest opposition parties Smer or HZDS, said leader of the ethnic Hungarian party SMK, Bela Bugar. SMK is a member of the current ruling coalition.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 2  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Martin Dokoupil on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging