\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to curb crown.   \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2004\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Dec 23 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a second day in a row on Thursday, and warned it would continue fighting to prevent the crown appreciating too quickly.   \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) has been battling against what it calls unjustified crown firming for more than a year, saying it could hurt the new EU member's economy.   \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to assess development of the crown's exchange rate, and if the dynamics of appreciation do not correspond to development of the economy, we will be ready to use monetary tools to correct such undesired movements," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown on Wednesday when the unit traded near its all-time highs at 38.550 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the NBS stepped into the market on Thursday when the crown was at around 38.700 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 This week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the first since July, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth a combined 766 million euros.   \par \par \uc2 The crown has risen rapidly against the euro this year, hitting a record high of 38.530 on Monday to notch up a 6.2 percent gain since January.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it does not oppose gradual crown firming based on improving productivity, and it expects a stronger crown in the longer term, but the monetary body wants to continue fighting inflows of speculative capital.   \par \par \uc2 Apart from direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also cut its main interest rates by a total of 200 basis points this year to make the crown less attractive for speculators who seek higher rates compared with major markets.   \par \par \uc2 The crown weakened to around 38.850-880 per euro after Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from 38.700, easing slightly less compared with the reaction in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said a major crown fall was unlikely in the near future as weaker levels attracted more crown buying from both domestic and foreign banks, which expect the unit to continue appreciating next year.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041223e0cn00bf6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
