\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown eases on second c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2004\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Dec 23 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown closed\par slightly weaker on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par for the second day in a row to push the unit to lower levels,\par dealers said.\par     The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) took advantage of\par lighter pre-holiday liquidity on Wednesday and Thursday and sold\par crowns on the market after repeated warnings that too fast an\par appreciation could hurt the economy.\par     The bank started \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday when the crown\par threatened to break 38.700 per euro, entering the market at a\par weaker rate compared with the starting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level of\par 38.550 in the previous session.\par     The crown ended at 38.830/870 to the euro, its main\par reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , compared with Wednesday's close of\par 38.720/750.\par     "It seems they (NBS) do not want to see it under 38.700 for\par the time being. On the other hand, they did not manage to push\par it through 38.900," one Bratislava-based dealer from a foreign\par bank said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I see the crown moving within that range next week. But the\par crown will gradually move to a stronger level again from the\par start of next year," he added.\par  \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have bought an estimated\par 300-500 million euros in the two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  days.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also warned on Thursday that it would stay\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prepared to correct crown movements in the future if the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation pace does not correspond to economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 development.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, analysts said they expected Slovakia's booming  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economy and inflows of foreign direct investment to fuel the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 crown's strengthening drive next year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We do not believe that the bank will manage to weaken the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 crown permanently, and (we) expect the rally to re-emerge in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 first quarter of next year at the latest, supported by rising  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 productivity and news about FDI inflows," Slovenska Sporitelna  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said in a market note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market will be closed for the Christmas holiday on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday, reopening on Monday for the last trading week of 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041223e0cn00fqs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
