\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , rand firm.  \b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2004\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown dropped off record highs against the euro on Wednesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the dollar's weak tone helped the South African rand hit fresh six-year highs.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen stepping in around 38.55 crowns per euro prompting a retreat to 38.90, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon recovered some of the lost ground as foreign banks resumed buying.  \par \par \uc2 The bank had warned at its policy meeting the previous day it would take action if crown movements did not reflect economic fundamentals, though analysts said it was fighting against an unstoppable tide of inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "Markets are completely dead at this time of year so it's easy to move the rate around, but I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will end up being successful," said Lars Christensen, emerging markets analyst at Danske Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been emphasising hot money flows, but the flows are real money. The reason the crown has gone so strong is that Slovakia has been pursuing the right economic policies.  \par \par \uc2 "They should be happy about that because it's putting a dampener on inflationary pressures."  \par \par \uc2 By 1038 GMT, the crown traded at 38.76 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Christensen said it seemed strange for the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just a day after revealing a switch to fixed inflation targeting.  \par \par \uc2 "It suggests they're pursuing two monetary policies, which is not really do-able."  \par \par \uc2 The bank's monetary programme for 2005-2008 set an end-2005 inflation target of 3.0-4.0 percent, down from the expected range of 5.7-7.0 percent for December 2004. Formerly, it had an implicit targeting system, when it only estimated price growth.  \par \par \uc2 "They should perhaps follow the Czech example of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but using interest rates to hit its inflation target."  \par \par \uc2 The rest of the central Europe region traded calmly with the Polish zloty hovering just under Tuesday's 22-month highs against the euro at around 4.10.  \par \par \uc2 RAND STEADY AFTER CPI  \par \par \uc2 The South African rand nudged to a fresh six-year high of 5.6505 per dollar in thin trade, showing little reaction to a faster-than-expected rise in inflation in November.  \par \par \uc2 South African November CPIX inflation rose at an annual pace of 4.6 percent, above a consensus forecast of 4.4 percent and up from 4.2 percent in October, going some way to justifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave rates on hold earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 "It was definitely higher than the market anticipated, but inflation could still start to dip as fuel price cuts start to feed through," said Razia Khan, chief Africa economist at Standard Chartered.  \par \par \uc2 "The number is not going to do much to change expectations on interest rates. If the rand remains strong, there could well be a rate cut in February."  \par \par \uc2 The rand was flat at 5.64 to the dollar .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041222e0cm00bf6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
