\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to slow crown firming.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca   \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2004\par 13:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, selling its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its long-lasting effort to prevent the rising crown from hurting the economy.   \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) has been trying to rein in the crown for more than a year, saying the unit's advance is too quick and does not correspond to fundamentals in the new EU member's economy.   \par \par \uc2 "We maintain what we have stated for several times," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat told Reuters. "The appreciation of the Slovak crown is too fast; the aim of the action was to slow down this movement."   \par \par \uc2 The crown has risen rapidly against the euro this year, hitting an all-time high of 38.530 to notch up a 6.2 percent gain since January.   \par \par \uc2 The unit was trading near record highs when the NBS entered the market on Wednesday, and the action briefly pulled the unit to 38.900 per euro. But the crown quickly rebounded and the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second time.   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first such direct action since July when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth a combined 766 million euros.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it does not oppose gradual crown firming based on improving productivity, but that it will continue to fight inflows of speculative capital.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS has cut rates by a total of 200 basis points this year to make the crown less attractive for speculators seeking higher yields than those on offer in major markets.   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came a day after a meeting at which it left its key two-week repo ceiling at 4.00 percent.   \par \par \uc2 MORE FIRMING SEEN   \par \par \uc2 Analysts have long questioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reasons for capping the crown's rise, saying the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is gaining due to solid economic growth and rising flows of foreign direct investment.   \par \par \uc2 "We believe that the direct \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have only short-term impact as fundamentals and FDI inflow will support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the course of 2005," Komercni Banka analysts said in market note. Bullish market sentiment was boosted further on Tuesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary programme for 2005-2008 showed predictions of accelerating economic growth in the next three years.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would switch to inflation targetting from 2005, setting the end-year target at 3.0-4.0 percent, compared with this year's estimate of 5.7-7.0 percent headline price growth.   \par \par \uc2 The monetary body will target inflation of under 2.5 percent in 2006 and below 2.0 percent in 2007 and 2008, which analysts said were ambitious goals.   \par \par \uc2 Some economists have warned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only achieve its long-term inflation goal, needed for euro adoption, with the help of a firming crown, and urged the bank to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate more freely.   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia plans to meet all criteria for joining the euro in 2007, so that it could adopt the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  two years later.   \par \par \uc2 "The NBS will need strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet its inflation target. We therefore suggest clients to take advantage of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy SKK (crowns)," Komercni Banka said.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041222e0cm00a16\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
