\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Dec 16.  \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2004\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK GOV SAYS WOULD APPROVE SKK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Outgoing \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Marian Jusko said he was in favour of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the crown's rapid appreciation and would approve the use of any the bank's tools if proposed by the board.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANKER MRVA SAYS SKK RISE TOO FAST  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown is firming too fast, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to use all of its tools to knock the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down if the rapid rise continues at its current pace, Karol Mrva, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member, told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 GOVT NOMINATES BARTO AS C.BANK VICE-GOV  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak government nominated Martin Barto as a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-governor, a former commercial banker who is expected to have a strong influence on monetary policy. Parliament is expected to vote in January on the nomination.  \par \par \uc2 ECON MIN SEES FDI INFLOW CONTINUING IN 2005  \par \par \uc2 Slovak Economy Minister Pavol Rusko said he expected foreign investors to continue flocking to the new EU member country next year with FDI seen at least at the same pace as in 2004. The ministry was hoping to finalise two large FDI projects in the near future, which should bring a total of 5,000 jobs to eastern Slovakia.  \par \par \uc2 KOUEI TO BUILD EUR 23 MLN RECYCLING UNIT  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak unit of Canada's Kouei Industries said on Wednesday, it planned to invest 22.5 million euros to build tyre and plastics recycling plants in central Slovakia.  \par \par \uc2 JOBLESS RATE DROPS TO 12.6 PCT IN NOV  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's unemployment rate fell for the tenth consecutive month in November, easing to 12.58 percent from 12.72 percent in the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Martin Dokoupil on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: martin.dokoupil.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041216e0cg005my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
