\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on August 2.  \b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2004\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Aug 2 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday:  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN TO RELEASE JAN-JULY STATE BUDGET DATA  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry will release the state budget data for the January-July period. Slovakia's state budget showed a deficit of 12.455 billion crowns in the first six months of this year. The 2004 state budget was approved with a ceiling for the deficit of 78.495 billion crowns.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK TO AUCTION 15-YR TREASURY BONDS  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold an auction of the third tranche of the 15-year, 5.30 percent treasury bonds on behalf of the finance ministry's debt and liquidity agency. The state sold 5.232 billion crowns worth of the paper at an average yield of 5.232 percent in the last tender on June 21. Total demand was 8.192 billion crowns.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK TO RELEASE JAN-MAY C/A DATA  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to release the current account data for the January-May period. The country's current account showed a surplus of 4.0 billion crowns in the first four months of the year.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK LEAVES RATES ON HOLD  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady on Friday, but kept the market on its toes by signalling willingness to ease the costs of credit further in light of muted price pressures. The decision, which left the main two-week repo rate at 4.50 percent, was widely expected by the markets due to the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent retreat to weaker levels.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK REVEALS COVERT \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  IN JUNE  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 87 million euro through a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deal in June, the bank said on Friday. The bank refrained from covert \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the strong crown in May and April, but bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth a combined 277 million euro in the first three months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 STATE BATTLES TO MEET KIA LAND HANDOVER DEADLINE  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia may not be able to hand over on time a construction site for a one billion euro ($1.2 billion) car plant of South Korea's auto maker Kia Motors , the economy ministry said on Friday. The state has run into difficulty purchasing land for the Kia plant, which will be the new EU member's largest ever greenfield foreign project, as several landowners refused to accept the price offered by the state.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DROP  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $13.321 billion in the week to July 28, from $13.530 billion one week earlier, the bank said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 For Slovak economic indicators  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Martin Dokoupil on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: martin.dokoupil.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click