\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Slovak cbank accepts all bids in 2-wk repo tender.  \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2004\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 20 (Reuters) - The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) accepted all bids in a two-week repo tender on Tuesday, surprising analysts who expected it to leave the market drowning in liquidity to weaken the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The NBS said it drained 90.999 billion crowns ($2.8 billion) of surplus liquidity from the money market, at an average rate of 4.41 percent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The market had eyed the outcome of the repo tender to gauge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reaction to the crown's quick recovery from six-weeks lows of 40.050 per euro it touched last week following massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Recently the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly rejected at least some bids to deter inflows of short-term capital, which is taking advantage of the interest rate differential with the euro zone. The NBS did not comment on the result of Tuesday's tender.  \par \par \uc2 The crown firmed to 39.801/851 per euro after the tender from the opening level of 39.845/895. Dealers said it was likely to test the key 39.800 per euro level in the coming days if the central bankers remain out of the market.  \par \par \uc2 "The crown firmed after the repo tender results. It seems that they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) accept that the crown could be a little stronger," said ING Bank dealer Jan Rafaj.  \par \par \uc2 Over the past week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to knock the crown off its record high of 39.675 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since erased most of its losses as the the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quit the market saying it was satisfied with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  result.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit, which is up 3.3 percent against the euro this year, has been firming sharply in the past months due to the country's solid economic performance and expectations of investment inflows from abroad.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the minimum rate was 4.20 percent, while the maximum accepted yield stood at 4.50 percent, matching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's limit rate for two-week tenders.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040720e07k001ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
