\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  changed trend.   \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2004\par 17:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Marian Jusko said on Wednesday he was satisfied with the outcome of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past week designed to halt a rapid firming of the crown.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last Thursday in the first such direct action since May 2003, and it continued to sell crowns on Monday and Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The bank knocked the crown off its the all-time high of 39.675 per euro, pushing the unit to around 39.910 in late Wednesday trading.   \par \par \uc2 "I am satisfied with the outcome of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Jusko told journalists after the regular government meeting.   \par \par \uc2 "There was a clear trend of excessive crown firming in the past few days and weeks and this tendency has been reversed," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak monetary body has been trying to slow crown appreciation for over a year, saying the firming has been too fast and could hurt the economy which entered the EU in May.   \par \par \uc2 Jusko said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered a wide range of issues when it decides on its policy moves.   \par \par \uc2 He said the possible negative impact of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on exporters was one of the factors, but not necessarily the main reason behind the latest action against the crown. "In recent past, we have met with 15 representatives of industrial chambers. There was not a single voice that would want a strong crown. The voices ware rather contrary," Jusko said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not disclose the amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  it had bought from the market, but the market estimated the volume at 400-500 million euros.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the initial fall of the crown, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  met stiff opposition from foreign banks at around 40.000 per euro as investors appeared to believe that the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had the potential to firm again.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might keep the crown off record highs for some time.   \par \par \uc2 But they predicted inflows of foreign capital to prevail in the long term due to Slovakia's good economic fundamentals, such as an improving trade balance, strong GDP growth and prospects of foreign direct investment projects.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040714e07e00244\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
