\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on July 14.  \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2004\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 14 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday:  \par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT HOLDS REGULAR MEETING  \par \par \uc2 The government will hold its weekly meeting. The agenda does not include major economic items. Financial markets will be watching the meeting to see whether \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, who attend government sessions, comment on recent crown moves.  \par \par \uc2 CEZ HOLDS NEWS CONFERENCE  \par \par \uc2 Czech dominant power producer CEZ will hold a news conference to speak about its plans in the privatisation tender for Slovak utility Slovenske Elektrarne.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY MINISTER MEETS EXPORTERS  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Pavol Rusko will present an award for Slovakia's best exporting company for 2003.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK CONTINUES TO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second consecutive day on Tuesday, continuing its fight against crown firming. The bank started selling crowns directly on the market on Thursday last week, saying it viewed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firming as too quick.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market on Tuesday when the crown traded near 39.900 per euro, which is a weaker level compared with the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rounds.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK DRAINS ALL EXCESS LIQUIDITY WITH REPO TENDER  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accepted all bids in its two-week repo tender on Tuesday, draining 114.92 billion crowns ($3.6 billion) of surplus liquidity from the market, the bank's data showed.  \par \par \uc2 MINISTRIES DEMAND MORE MONEY FROM 2005 BUDGET  \par \par \uc2 Slovak ministries are demanding more funds for the so-called priority projects for 2005 than the allocated sum in the preliminary budget draft. The finance ministry said that total demands exceed the budgeted amount by 22 billion crowns.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1  \par \par \uc2 For Slovak economic indicators  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040714e07e0011b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
