\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown slides as cbank keeps  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2004\par 17:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, July 13 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown ended\par weaker on Tuesday, hit by the third wave of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at undermining the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's firming\par potential, dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Tuesday\par for the third time in less than a week, trying to weaken the\par crown through a psychological level of 40.000 per euro.\par  "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started buying euros as soon as the crown\par touched 39.900 (per euro) and it succeeded in sending it up to\par 40.035," said ING Bank dealer Jan Rafaj.\par     Market watchers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have bought\par around 100 million euros on Tuesday, less than the 200 million\par it was estimated to have bought in each of the previous\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rounds on Monday and Thursday.\par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was probably aiming to push\par the crown beyond the next strong level of 40.100 per euro,\par hoping that it would trigger a wave of stop-loss orders.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think that 40.100 (per euro) level will be defended very\par strongly and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not push the crown\par through it alone," Rafaj said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par after interest rate cuts and money market tools failed to\par discourage foreign capital inflows and reverse crown firming.\par     Traders said the crown could float in a range of\par 39.900-40.050 per euro in the coming days, but added that\par investors would keep testing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's determination to\par fight market flows with direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Analysts have said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's attempts to stop the\par surging crown would have only a temporary impact as the\par country's sound economic performance was likely to keep\par attracting foreign investors.\par --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1430 GMT--------------------\par Crown/euro  at 39.948/997 at 39.900/940 on Monday\par Crown/dollar  at 32.396/446 from 32.145/195\par 5-yr yield March 2008  at 4.304/102 pct vs 4.274/074\par 10-yr yld July 2013  at 5.075/4.932 pct vs 4.989/883\par ----------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040713e07d001u1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
