\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to weaken crown.   \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2004\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second consecutive day on Tuesday, continuing its fight against crown firming.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat confirmed Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he declined to give any details about the action.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling crowns directly on the market on Thursday last week, saying it viewed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firming since the beginning of the year as too quick.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market on Tuesday when the crown traded near 39.900 per euro, which is a weaker level compared with the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rounds.   \par \par \uc2 "This time, it started when it looked that the crown could go under 39.900 (per euro)... It seems they are trying to move the crown above 40.000," one Bratislava-based dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 This month's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the first direct action on the market since May 2003, but the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been fighting against crown firming for more than a year.   \par \par \uc2 It has used interest rate cuts and money market instruments to discourage inflows of foreign capital, saying that that gains which are too sharp could hurt the small and open economy that joined the European Union in May.   \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit to 40.030 per euro. The crown hit an all-time high of 39.675 per euro last week, which was around 3.7 percent up from the beginning of the year.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considers the crown's rally to be fuelled by inflows of speculative capital, but many analysts say foreign investors are attracted mainly by Slovakia's good economic fundamentals. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said there will be some room for crown firming in the long term, but it added that it would continue using its monetary arsenal to prevent sharp market moves.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040713e07d000vu\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Slovak near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\in